ad","required":false,"type":"int"}],"price":1,"resource":"credit","schema_version":1,"source":{"attribution":"Source: FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis; federalreserve.gov","hosts":["api.stlouisfed.org"],"licence":"FRED API terms of use; the FOMC calendar is a US government work","publisher":"Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis (FRED release calendar); Federal Reserve Board (FOMC calendar)","terms_status":"verify before production (FRED API terms)","terms_url":"https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/terms_of_use.html"},"text_is_untrusted":false,"title":"US release calendar"},{"available":true,"cache_ttl_seconds":3600,"description":"A central bank's policy rate (BIS, with the date and size of its last change; the Fed's target range from FRED; Brazil's Selic target from the BCB; Canada's target from the Bank of Canada Valet API) and its next scheduled decision dates. Covers FED, ECB, BOJ, BOE, BCB, SNB, RBA, BOC, BOI, or all.","id":"cb_policy_rates","key":{"file":"fred.key","optional":true},"output":"data: today, what, banks {CODE: {bank, policy_rate_pct, rate_as_of, rate_effective_from, previous_rate_pct, last_change_bps, target_range_pct, selic_target_pct, next_decision, upcoming_decisions, last_scheduled_decision_in_table, calendar_source, schedule_status (scheduled, or unknown with the reason in calendar_note), rate_available, rate_may_be_stale, ...}} (one entry, or every bank for all), calendar_staleness_warning","params":[{"doc":"FED, ECB, BOJ, BOE, BCB, SNB, RBA, BOC, BOI, a common name (Brazil, Copom, FOMC), or all","max_bytes":64,"name":"bank","pattern":"^[\\p{L}\\p{N} .,'&()/+:-]+$","required":true,"type":"string"},{"default":"both","doc":"rate, next_meeting (no upstream request) or both","enum":["rate","next_meeting","both"],"name":"what","required":false,"type":"enum"}],"price":1,"resource":"credit","schema_version":1,"source":{"attribution":"BIS central bank policy rates (WS_CBPOL); Banco Central do Brasil; FRED; Bank of Canada Valet API; Bank of England; European Central Bank; Reserve Bank of Australia","hosts":["stats.bis.org","api.bcb.gov.br","api.stlouisfed.org","www.bankofcanada.ca","www.bankofengland.co.uk","www.ecb.europa.eu","www.rba.gov.au"],"licence":"BIS statistics: free reuse with attribution; BCB open data; FRED terms for the target range; Bank of Canada Valet: terms at https://www.bankofcanada.ca/terms/ — free reuse with attribution","publisher":"Bank for International Settlements (policy rates); Banco Central do Brasil (SGS 432); FRED (Fed target range); Bank of Canada Valet API (series V39079); the Bank of England's Bank Rate page, the ECB's key interest rates page and the RBA's cash rate table when BIS lags a decision; each bank's published calendar","terms_status":"verify before production (BIS, BCB, Bank of Canada Valet terms; calendars need a yearly refresh)","terms_url":"https://www.bis.org/terms_statistics.htm"},"text_is_untrusted":false,"title":"Central-bank policy rates and decision dates"},{"available":true,"cache_ttl_seconds":3600,"description":"Model estimates before the official print: Atlanta Fed GDPNow, New York Fed Staff Nowcast (with 50% and 80% bands) and Cleveland Fed inflation nowcasts (CPI, core CPI, PCE, core PCE, month over month and year over year), each with latest and previous values, as-of dates and target period.","id":"us_nowcasts","key":{"file":"fred.key","optional":true},"output":"data: economy (US), measure, nowcasts[] (name, measure, target_period, latest_value, latest_as_of, next_update, previous_value, previous_as_of, bands_pct, series, source_url), partial (true when a source failed: nowcasts[] lacks its estimates), source_errors[]","params":[{"default":"all","doc":"gdp, inflation or all","enum":["gdp","inflation","all"],"name":"measure","required":false,"type":"enum"}],"price":1,"resource":"credit","schema_version":1,"source":{"attribution":"Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta GDPNow; Federal Reserve Bank of New York Staff Nowcast; Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland i